{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/307849-will-the-shuankhsen-ever-get-the-player-treatment","id":307849,"title":"Will the Shuankhsen ever get the player treatment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-09T21:04:22-08:00","id":307849,"title":"Will the Shuankhsen ever get the player treatment?","content":"I've always thought the Shuankhsen were the most sympathetic sort of Mummy, and Book of the Deceived's excellent take on the Akhem-Urtu just makes me think that an attempt at Ammut's favorites as protagonists would be fantastic. Between their incredibly shit luck (slaves, foreigners, and criminals versus the effectively &quot;middle class&quot; of the Guilds, brutlly murdered rather than ritually sacrificed) and how Ammut could be presented somewhat ambiguously (just look at some Wraith material on Oblivion and Spectres), I'd love to see this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:16:55-08:00","id":307907,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone is lower in Irem than the people who became the Shuankhsen, and I definitely think they could use some expansion. Maybe we could brainstorm some movements, sort of like the ones that appeared in the Deceived book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:28:36-08:00","id":307908,"title":"","content":"The main reason I'm not as interested in the Shuankhsen is the fact that they don't have Memory as a morality stat - which, incidentally, makes them great antagonists in that they remember everything, which I suppose is precisely the intention <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:32:02-08:00","id":307910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/307849-will-the-shuankhsen-ever-get-the-player-treatment?p=307908#post307908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main reason I'm not as interested in the Shuankhsen is the fact that they don't have Memory as a morality stat - which, incidentally, makes them great antagonists in that they remember everything, which I suppose is precisely the intention <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a new behavioral stat would be appropriate - maybe one that ties into their relationship with Ammut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T22:43:54-08:00","id":307911,"title":"","content":"Oh, I think morality is perfect in that it's the most thematically appropriate - it's just that it's also less <i>interesting </i>than memory. <br /> <br /> The Shuankhsen remember everything - this makes them fantastic antagonists. They're less powerful than the Arisen, individually, but they will always adapt better to the future than the Arisen, they will never be as confused, and they know precisely what you did last century. <br /> <br /> In a way, the basic themes of Mummy - memory, the quest for self-knowledge and understanding, isolation from humanity, etc., don't apply to the Shuankhsen. Which, yeah. Great antagonist material. Not so interesting as PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:38:35-08:00","id":307953,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Leave them their fallen status. I admit a story or two about trying to 'fix' one, maybe turning one into an Arisen or (better yet) one of the Deceived would be interesting but not as a protagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T01:04:37-08:00","id":307976,"title":"","content":"There is something to be said for playing the fallen and the damned. The Shaunkhsen are pretty darn tragic in both back-story and execution within game if used well by an ST. <br /> <br /> They have an inherent conflict in them, they are in some ways far more &quot;human&quot; then the Arisen, since they have their memories perfectly intact from their mortal days. Yet their have the dark urges of the Devourer polluting their minds and driving them towards terrible deeds.This means their morality is always on a downward spiral, they might be able to stabilize around Morality 1-3. However, its incredible hard for them to climb back up as their very nature is fighting them.<br /> <br /> They collect mortals in cults as the Arisen do, but treat them as more disposable. Even if a Shaunkhsen try their best to treat there follows with any sort of greater emotional investment, the simple fact is that the pull of Ammut and necessity of their nature will make them betray and destroy. Even between individual Shaunkhsen their will be tensions, the stronger will always dominant the weaker. Those who have been more successful will likely form a hierarchy over their lessers to maximize their reach in the world. Meanwhile these &quot;lessers&quot; will likely gain resources and protection from the more powerful members of society. Though of course they will ever hunger to take the place of those above them in this predatory pecking order. <br /> <br /> A game focused on the Shaunkhsen about how these undead (lifeless) beings with an inner conflict between their human personality and their ever hungering damnation. Meanwhile the outer conflict will be between the tension that naturally occurs when such a group of predators even tries to form a coherent social group and deal with its enemies. This all sounds like a solid premise for a lot of stories to me.<br /> <br /> Oh wait, we already have game like that.<br /> <br /> Its called Vampire the Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T02:33:30-08:00","id":308001,"title":"","content":"I believe we have enough information on the Shuanksem that you can play them already just using the corebook. We have their on rules on the Silence, how they regain pillar points or obtain dots, the Morality stats and Bane Affinities. That they have cults, the Fasad, there's already loads of material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:38:40-08:00","id":308161,"title":"","content":"It could be interesting to play one, but if it's dark, evil Mummies you want to play then <b>Book of the </b><b>Deceived</b> just came out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> There's a line in there that mentions how the Deceived view the Arisen as <i>enemies</i>, but they're not <i>monsters</i> like the Shuankhsen. And...yeah. What would you do with them as PCs that you couldn't do with the Arisen (the quest for Apotheosis) or the Deceived (the quest of being evil and fighting other Mummies)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}